5. the correction to item 8, quantified
================================================================================================================================
  canonical  the h8 EFE recipe [nu evaluated at the TRUE external field, no (1+L) factor] gives dispersions +0.046 dex (1.11x) different from the QUMOND eq.-60 recipe used here; h8's centring Upsilon_V should therefore be read as 0.81x its printed value
  alt        the h8 EFE recipe [nu evaluated at the TRUE external field, no (1+L) factor] gives dispersions +0.055 dex (1.14x) different from the QUMOND eq.-60 recipe used here; h8's centring Upsilon_V should therefore be read as 0.77x its printed value
  the factor-2 warning in h8 is REAL but applies only in the EFE-DOMINATED limit (check V2 above).  Local Group satellites are not deeply in that limit -- their own internal field is comparable to the host's -- so on THIS data the two prescriptions
  differ by only +0.046 dex in sigma.  h8's headline number is therefore not an artefact of its EFE recipe; the gap between h8's printed Upsilon_V = 23.8 and this script's 62.9 is a SAMPLE effect (this run adds 31 ultra-faints that h8's catalogue did not carry) plus the 4/3 deprojection of r_half.
  [PASS] 8-CORR bookkeeping, reported against my own expectation: I expected the corrected QUMOND external-field formula to remove much of item 8's liability, and it does NOT -- on Local Group satellites the two prescriptions agree to ~0.05 dex, because these systems are not deeply EFE-dominated.  Item 8's liability stands, and is confirmed here on a 2x larger and newer sample   (prescription difference +0.046 dex in sigma (1.24x in Upsilon_V); corrected all-MW centring Upsilon_V = 62.9 on N=45, MW-classical-only 10.2 on N=14 (h8 printed 23.8 on 46 Local Group dwarfs, mostly classical))

